  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered"><span class="username">Chamilka</span>, You Are The <span class="archetype">Innocent</span> - <span class="text-orange">And This Is What It Means...</span></h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/it-means.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>Before you dismiss this Archetypal introduction as nothing but hogwash, you must know that the Innocent archetype is NOT one that's typically associated with naivety. Truth be told, it is anything but. If you'd like to find out the truth about what the Innocent really resembles, then please proceed with the rest of this Archetypal Introduction with <span class="text-orange">an open mind, and a willing heart</span>.</p>
              <p>The Innocent archetype is best defined by its sheer positivity, enthusiasm, and optimism. They're able to interpret any situation in a perspective that's hopeful, encouraging, and infectious. If you're thinking that there's a lot more to the Innocent archetype than just that, you're exactly right!</p>
              <p>Individuals of the Innocent archetype, including you, tend to see the silver lining in every cloud and are constantly reminding themselves that there's virtue and a sense of goodness in everything, and every situation. You're always on the lookout for wisdom and lessons worth learning, no matter how painful your experiences get...</p>
              <p>To you, <span class="username"></span>, everyone has a story worth listening to, every circumstance holds something worth experiencing, and everything that happens in life, happens for a reason. That is a belief; a <span class="text-orange">deep-rooted outlook</span> that makes the Innocent archetype so remarkable.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Your archetype also suggests that there is a side of you that's relentless... Relentless in the sense of striving to improve yourself - whether it's your physical abilities, your mental fortitude, or your emotional resilience.</p>
          <p>That being said, you're certainly an individual of impressive characteristics - characteristics that are unique to your archetype.</p>
          <p>You seem to exercise selflessness in everything that you do... No matter how small or minuscule your actions appear to be, every decision that you make, no matter how small, is always for a purpose that serves others. And when it comes to making important and difficult decisions, you're <span class="text-orange">assertive, firm, and steadfast</span>.</p>
          <p>Your archetype also suggests that you're simple, easy-going, and transparent. You're the type of person who's willing to wear your heart on your sleeve, stand up for your beliefs, and face the consequences of mistakes... An upstanding individual who's fearless in profound ways.</p>
          <p>Amongst all the archetypes, you tend to have the purest of intentions... And that's best illustrated through the way you interact with others. Unlike others, when you claim to be happy for someone else, you actually do mean it from the bottom of your heart - and that goes a long way in forging valuable, close relationships.</p>
          <p>You might not like to admit it... But when things don't turn out your way, you're easily disappointed. That, of course, does not mean to say that your spoilt... It's that your positive outlook on everything can sometimes set you up for disappointments. But that's the price you have to pay for possessing such a <span class="text-orange">unique set of strengths</span>.</p>
          <p>The Innocent archetype is such a joy to be around, and I have no doubt that your friends and loved ones will agree with this. Your light-hearted and jovial nature make you fun-loving, charismatic, and likeable.</p>
          <p>You try not to be serious most of the time, and you enjoy engaging in little things that will make someone else's day brighter. Whether it's pretending to laugh at a corny joke, applauding a predictable magic trick, you'd very much rather bless that person with positivity than put them down.</p>
          <p>And that's just a small piece of the puzzle that forms the entirety of the <span class="text-orange">wonderful, angelic individual</span> that you are. Unlike the archetypes who tend to struggle with hatred and animosity, you'd very much rather make friends than enemies. You're accepting, kind, and incredibly thoughtful.</p>
          <p>You might not be aware of this... But all of these personality traits lead to so much more. Your optimism makes you ferocious - like an unstoppable force.</p>
          <p>There is no archetype that matches your level of determination, because there is nothing stronger than an unbreakable spirit.</p>
          <p>That's why the world needs more people like you, <span class="username"></span> ... I have no doubt that you will one day infect others with your positivity, and influence them to have the same tenacity as you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Innocent</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Hidden Qualities, Unknown Tendencies,<br>And Positive Attributes</span> That You Wouldn't Expect</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/abilities.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>The Innocent archetype is one of the most socially adept archetypes out there. Unsurprisingly, they are also quite extroverted. They tend to thrive when there are people around them because they take in all the emotional energy of society then channel it into their own selves.</p>
              <p>Naturally, this makes you quite jolly and actually <span class="text-orange">optimistic about life’s problems</span>. You do not see problems as long-lasting or things that worry you. In fact, you don’t even let the problems get to you at all. They’re like storms that pass, and typically you can get anywhere by having this mindset.</p>
              <p>Add to that, you tend to gravitate towards people and being with others. You see people as a source of strength and simply seeing a couple of your dear friends is enough to make your day. You are also a team-player, putting the needs of others above even your own if it means just seeing things through and becoming better for others in the process.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>More importantly, one of your most prominent qualities is your intuition. This means that while you understand the place that logic has in a society, there are times when gut feeling and giving people the benefit of the doubt is the right course of action. The fact that you use this more often than not compliments your social traits. Of course, there are times when you are wrong about your assessments of the situation, but things nevertheless end up working in your favor.</p>
          <p>Also, you are a turbulent character who likes to often move around. You regularly prefer talking to people and hearing their stories, understanding in the <span class="text-orange">process their perspectives</span> and then integrating them into your own.</p>
          <p>However, this also makes you quite anxious and vulnerable, frequently doubting yourself and relying on the other people around you for validation. This validation can be cyclical and can end up hurting you more often than it can improve you.</p>
          <p>That being said, there’s more about your potential than you understand at this juncture, <span class="username"></span>. </p>
          <p>With your hidden qualities in full view, it is time for you to know what your strengths are and how you can better use them...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-1" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(1,2)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step2">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Innocent, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Hidden Strengths And<br>Positive Attributes</span> That You Wouldn't Expect</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/abilities-2.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>As an Innocent, you are highly sociable. Your positive aura that draws people in. Whereas the Jester excites others by cracking jokes and aiming to make them happy, you exude that <span class="text-orange">undying optimism</span> that makes people believe in themselves. </p>
              <p>This strength often goes underrated. When people communicate and socialize, there’s this underlying notion that they compare themselves with others. And the sad reality is this – some (or even most) of us find a twisted sense of self-worth when others are in a lower position. Why do you think people love watching reality TV shows? Why are people entertained with the suffering and struggles of others? </p>
              <p>However, socializing with you is different. People feel empowered. They are moved by your energy. They don’t feel insecure or threatened. Instead, they are inspired by your ideas and visions, making you extremely likeable. As an extrovert, you do not carry that condescending vibe. Instead, you are someone who constantly uplifts, even those who don’t believe in themselves anymore. </p>
              <p>Moreover, as a we-centered archetype, you are empathetic. You easily relate to the situation of others since you see them in relation to your own. You’re <span class="text-orange">never trapped in your own bubble</span> as you relate to the world in ways that you can. Thus, you constantly reach out to help and inspire those around you.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Add to that, this empathetic nature also allows you to see the situation for what it is. Oftentimes, your archetype is criticized for being naïve and unrealistic. However, experienced Innocents can use their empathy to ground themselves and make sure that they’re standing on firm footing. </p>
          <p>When you are able to achieve this, you won’t become too much of an idealist. Because of your empathy, you can connect with others and relate to their struggles. This will empower you to find the best solution out there, to a point of leading you to go beyond yourself. Thus, don’t be afraid to utilize this strength as this is one of your core bases. </p>
          <p>Unlike other archetypes, you <span class="text-orange">stand out as a self-improver</span>. Stemming from your turbulent personality, you are always emphatically moved by your own inaptness. Meaning, when a situation arises, and you’re unable to do something, this angers you and moves you to take action. </p>
          <p>Doing everything necessary, you will stop at nothing in order to gain the skills that you need. This will require time and dedication on your end, but it won’t faze you from moving forward. </p>
          <p>As such, you’ll gain skills from almost all aspects of life. Just like the Jester, you can quickly become a jack of all trades and even a master of all. By constantly challenging yourself to break boundaries, you continually go further. </p>
          <p>With that, this strength of self-improving becomes evident to those around you. And as you develop yourself further, you’ll inspire others to move in your direction. </p>
          <p>Finally, as an Innocent, your <span class="text-orange">intuitive nature allows you to be trustful</span>. Generally, what this means is having that inner faith that things will work. From having that trust in systems, having confidence in your peers, or even counting on yourself, your ability to trust is second to none. </p>
          <p>With this strength, you’ll find it easier to face and conquer challenges that are naturally bigger than you. Since you have an inner trust that things will work out fine, you’re never afraid to cross borders and challenge stereotypes. This creates a dynamic personality in you, something that attracts others to take action as well.</p>
          <p>More importantly, this inner trust will also move you to become stronger from within. Regardless of how others may mock you or count you out, your trust converts into self-confidence. </p>
          <p>Now that you’re acquainted with your strengths, dear <span class="username"></span>, it is time for you to know how you can exercise them in various aspects of your life. </p>
          <p>For now, let’s start with one that strikes a chord: your romantic relationships.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-2" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(2,3)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual text-left pb-3 pt-5" id="step3">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;" class="long-title">
            <h3 class="centered">As A Innocent, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Relationship Qualities</span> That Are Within You</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-4">
              <img src="../assets/images/relationship.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <p>Due to your Turbulent nature, you tend to trust your partner in a snap. Whereas other archetypes need to constantly verify things, you are inclined to allowing your gut to lead the way. </p>
              <p>This tendency is certainly tricky. Whereas trust is ultimately necessary for a healthy relationship, it can also act as a double-edged sword. Just as how trust can easily be broken by the <span class="text-orange">smallest of lies</span>, such a tendency of yours can become detrimental if left unchecked. </p>
              <p>For instance, this tendency can lead you to become complacent to your partner. Trusting that they will do what’s right, you might be giving them too much freedom to the point of neglect. As such, they can interpret it differently and indirectly allow for moments of infidelity. While such is not your fault, this could have been averted if you’ve had a wider perspective on things instead of simply putting faith in it. </p>
              <p>Moreover, this tendency can also <span class="text-orange">shatter your expectations</span>. The thing about relationships is that the standards we expect from others are often the standards we set upon ourselves. Whereas you see yourself as someone who’s truly trustworthy, such a dangerous predicament may lead to seeing the same way on your partner even when that’s not the reality. </p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>As such, make sure to trust your partner, albeit in a more balanced way. Challenges will naturally surface, and the mutual trust between the two of you will constantly be tested. Instead of simply leaving things out to them, make sure to constantly check on things. As Ronald Reagan once said, “trust, but verify.” </p>
          <hr class="dashed">
          <p>Gratefulness is often an underrated tendency in relationships. In a world filled with instant gratification and unwarranted entitledness, some feel that we automatically deserve love and must be served on a silver platter. If not, this market-driven society allows us to purchase such love using money as a currency. </p>
          <p>But as a genuine lover, you <span class="text-orange">exhibit gratefulness</span>. And by this, what we mean is outright voicing out how much you appreciate being on the receiving end. As your partner prepares surprises for you, you’re never short of words and actions to express how lucky you are to receive them. </p>
          <p>Such gratefulness stems from your we-centeredness. Since you understand the importance of the connection between you and your partner, you show this value by letting them know that you’re happy with them. By doing so, you are actively empowering positivity within the relationship, moving each other to better and greater heights. </p>
          <p>More importantly, you also show your gratefulness through actions as well. Instead of simply saying words of appreciation, you replicate the acts of love and kindness by doing your own. In this way, you are letting your partner know how much you value them. </p>
          <p>Given such, it is important to remain steadfast on this quality as others may perceive you with <span class="text-orange">jealously and ill-mindedness</span>. Try to keep things private and avoid overdoing things by posting too much online. People may perceive it negatively, whereas you’re just being yourself – the grateful you.</p>
          <p>As you know, however, the Innocent is not just about romance and love. Indeed, there’s another aspect in your life where you can apply yourself, <span class="username"></span>. </p>
          <p>Without further ado, it’s time to see where you can take yourself in your career.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
          <a class="btn btn-outline-success btn-3" id="nav-btn2" onclick="nextReading(3,4)">Show Me Now</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step4">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Innocent</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Potential Career Paths</span></h3>
          </div>
          <p>Generally, the Innocent is a combination of extroversion, intuitiveness, we-centeredness, and turbulence. This makes up for strong career paths in relation to politics, health services, and legal jurisprudence. With their idealistic nature, an Innocent can blossom in these paths. And while these are suggestive of what you can pursue with your strengths, know that you should never limit yourself to them. </p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/politic.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Politics</h5>
              <p>With their uniqueness, an Innocent is best suited as a politician. Because they have the natural knack to sell a dream, they’ll find it natural to convince others towards their ideals. </p>
              <p>As an Innocent, you seek to lead others to success. And what better way to do this apart from being a politician yourself? Able to emphatically and empathetically engage with your audience, you can slowly work your way through the White House. </p>
              <p>Since you are the type who seeks the best of all, politics is often the most optimal way for you to achieve your dreams. By having the power to shape governments and its constituents, this is the perfect career for you to actualize your ideals. Instead of simply submitting to the system, you can ideally alter it from the inside and pursue the utopian society that you’re aspiring for.  </p>
              <p>Be careful, though. There is a reason why the wisest man in Athens, Socrates, decided not to enter politics. As a vicious and treacherous road, politics can sway you to become the very person you’ve sought to defeat. Doubtful? Go binge watch Frank Underwood’s quest in the House of Cards, and you’ll see what I mean.  </p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Even then, don’t give up just yet. If there’s someone fitted to traverse this road to hell, you are definitely that person. Unlike the Ruler archetype, whose very prone to corruption, your biggest strength is clinging to your own ideals. And in times of trials, this will truly help you make the right decisions, no matter the cost. Instead of simply settling for band-aid solutions, the win-win perspective in you, together with your moral fiber, will push you to achieve your goals.  </p>

          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/health-service.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Health Services</h5>
              <p>Health services is one of the key areas where you can become effective. As an archetype, you are naïve, even to the point of purity. Given such, this notion affects how you perceive life and how you think it should go along.  </p>
              <p>As such, having a career in the health services is a good way for you to live your life. Naturally passionate to help others, the Innocent in you can empower you to take on the challenges of pursuing the arduous road of medicine. Whether you become a nurse, doctor, or even pharmacist, the level of idealism that’s needed in these professions is close to none. </p>
              <p>More importantly, pursuing a career in health services requires having both ideals and the heart of service. While other archetypes may lack these, you as an Innocent is perfect for such qualifiers. As you pursue your career in this sector, you’ll feel the imminent desire to attain the best results possible. </p>
              <p>Add to that, you are also known to be resilient. You simply won’t give up. You will stop at nothing in achieving what you want. As such, this will push you forward, even when the road is bleak and winding. After all, a career in the field of medicine will have endless twist and turns. </p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Even then, your resilience will prove as useful. And in doing so, you also get to inspire others towards your mission. Through your concrete actions in this field, people will be moved by your actualized ideals and the outright positive energy that you exude.  </p>

          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/legal-jurisprudence.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Legal Jurisprudence</h5>
              <p>Unbeknownst to many, Innocents are actually great in the field of legal jurisprudence. Since they are naturally idealists and extroverts, they often get a good grasp of what needs to be done in order to achieve a certain goal. Although they are portrayed as naïve and gullible, a seasoned Innocent can hamper these weaknesses and instead harness the power of reason and logic.</p>
              <p>As an Innocent, you are naturally born with the ability to think through things. And unlike the Sage, who uses their godlike intellect, you power your way through by your sheer amount of optimism. Unrivaled in your desire to move towards the direction you want, legal jurisprudence is something that perfectly suits you.</p>
              <p>Just as what Friedrich Nietzsche said, “He who has the why to live, can bear with almost any how.” And for the Innocent, the raison d’etre or reason for living is as clear as day. Even when the sun is out, the radiance of their ideals still shines upon them, as if to say that these thoughts where solid representations of ideals from Plato’s world of forms.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Given this unparalleled willpower, you can pursue the career on legal jurisprudence. Despite being tricky and treacherous, you perfectly fit this long and arduous road since you have the ability to generate your own energy to move forward.</p>
          <p>And as you reach higher heights in this career, you can impact society in as much as a politician can. In fact, you can even transition to become a politician and author some worthwhile bills that can positively impact the lives of the many. If not, you can become a lawyer who will protect what’s right and moral.</p>
          <p>But while your career prospects certainly glimmer with the hope of prosperity, there are uncomfortable truths about yourself that you will need to face. The first of which will be no more comforting, <span class="username"></span>, and it is this...</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-12 text-center">
